<!--
    Copyright (c) 2026 Splitwirez
    Licensed under the MIT License. See LICENSE-aero-theme-for-avalonia.txt in the Themes/Aero
    directory for the full text of the copyright notice and permission notice.
    Source: https://github.com/Splitwirez/aero-theme-for-avalonia at main = a705b7c0
            src/AeroAvalonia/AVMAP/StyleTrailMix.axaml
    Changes from upstream:
      1. NARROWED the surviving PART_ContentPresenter rule. Upstream writes it as
         ":is(TemplatedControl):disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter" -
         app-wide, not Aero-scoped. Fluent's ComboBoxItem also names its presenter
         PART_ContentPresenter, and Views/Settings/AppearanceCard.axaml.cs:146-148 makes the font
         list's group captions non-selectable by setting IsEnabled=false AND a grey Foreground on
         the ComboBoxItem itself; unnarrowed, this rule would repaint those captions to
         AeroDisabledForeground behind that code's back, because a TextBlock.Foreground on the
         presenter beats a Foreground inherited from the item. The subject is therefore the six
         concrete types this project gives an Aero template, spelled out one by one. An Avalonia
         type selector is an EXACT type match (only :is() widens to subclasses), so CheckBox,
         ToggleSwitch, ToggleButton and RepeatButton each have to be named even though all four
         derive from Button.
      5. DELETED the :not(:disabled) twin of that rule (upstream lines 43-45). Two independent
         reasons, either sufficient. First, it does not compile here: its value is
         "{Binding Foreground, RelativeSource={RelativeSource Mode=TemplatedParent}}", and this
         project builds with AvaloniaUseCompiledBindingsByDefault, under which a TemplatedParent
         RelativeSource outside a ControlTemplate is Avalonia error AVLN2100 - observed, not
         predicted. The escapes are {ReflectionBinding} or x:CompileBindings="False", and this round
         forbids the first outright and the second would reintroduce it by the back door on a
         NativeAOT build. Second, the rule is a no-op: TemplatedControl.ForegroundProperty IS
         TextElement.ForegroundProperty.AddOwner<TemplatedControl>(), and TextElement's is
         registered with inherits:true (decompiled from Avalonia.Controls 12.1.0), so the presenter
         already resolves the templated parent's Foreground by inheritance. Setting it explicitly
         restates what inheritance produces. The :disabled rule below is NOT redundant in the same
         way - it names a brush the parent does not have - which is why it is kept.
      2. DELETED every rule keyed on the CSS class "aeroState" (upstream lines 9-13, 15-26, 27-38 and
         40-42). That class is applied to no element anywhere in the upstream repository - only
         "aeroState2" is - so the opacity cross-fade machinery those rules drive never runs. The
         design document's dead-list names lines 9,10,11,15,16,17,18,27,28,29,30, which are the
         eleven SELECTOR CLAUSES of the first three rules; it omits the fourth rule at 40-42, whose
         selector "Border.aeroState.disabled" is dead for exactly the same reason. Counted here
         against the file, not copied from the list.
      3. DELETED the ":is(Shape).aeroState2" transition rule (upstream 69-76). aeroState2 is applied
         to Border elements only, in all five upstream files that use it; no Shape carries it.
      4. DELETED the commented-out AeroFadeOutDuration transition block (upstream 59-68) and, with
         it, the now-unreferenced AeroFadeOutDuration key (upstream line 6). That block was the key's
         only consumer anywhere upstream.
    What is left is the two rules that do something, and the one resource they need. The design
    document predicts three; change 5 is why it is two, and the third rule it counted is the one
    that cannot compile under this project's binding settings.
    Everything else is byte for byte upstream.
-->
<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:ClassModifier="Internal">
    <Styles.Resources>
        <x:TimeSpan x:Key="AeroFadeDuration">0:0:0.125</x:TimeSpan>
    </Styles.Resources>

    <Style Selector="Button:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter,
                    RepeatButton:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter,
                    ToggleButton:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter,
                    CheckBox:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter,
                    ToggleSwitch:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter,
                    ListBoxItem:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
        <Setter Property="TextBlock.Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource AeroDisabledForeground}"/>
    </Style>

    <Style Selector=":is(TemplatedControl) /template/ Border.aeroState2">
        <Setter Property="Transitions">
            <Transitions>
                <BrushTransition Property="Background" Duration="{StaticResource AeroFadeDuration}" />
                <BrushTransition Property="BorderBrush" Duration="{StaticResource AeroFadeDuration}" />
            </Transitions>
        </Setter>
    </Style>
</Styles>
